    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis bright and spacious two-bedroom apartment is situated within Granitefield Manor, a mature and well-maintained private development of quality apartments in a popular and convenient suburban location.\n\nThe property benefits from a thoughtful layout, well-proportioned accommodation and excellent natural light throughout. The apartment is well appointed and is likely to appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike.\n\nGranitefield Manor enjoys an excellent location within easy reach of Dún Laoghaire, Monkstown, Killiney, Cherrywood and Sandyford Business District, while also offering convenient access to the City Centre and the M50. The development is well served by public transport, with excellent bus services nearby, making commuting both easy and practical.\n\nA wide choice of local amenities is available in the surrounding area, including Killiney Shopping Centre, nearby cafés, shops and everyday services. There are also numerous recreational facilities close at hand, including local parks, coastal walks, sports clubs and leisure amenities, all of which add to the appeal of this well-regarded location..."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nWood flooring, telephone intercom to hall door and large hot press.\n\nLiving Room: - \nBright and spacious reception room with wood flooring, timber fireplace with marble hearth and inset electric fire. Door to balcony, south-east facing aspect. Archway to kitchen.\n\nStorage Closet/Utility Area: - \nWashing machine with shelving.\n\nKitchen: - \nWood flooring, range of built-in floor and eye-level units with worktop space and tiled splashback. Built-in Beko oven, four-ring ceramic hob with extractor hood over and integrated dishwasher.\n\nMaster Bedroom: - \nSpacious double bedroom with extensive range of built-in wardrobes.\n\nEn-Suite: - \nFully tiled shower cubicle, wash hand basin, w/c, extractor and electric heater.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nGenerous double bedroom with built-in wardrobes and door to balcony.\n\nMain Bathroom: - \nFully tiled bath with shower attachment over, wash hand basin, w/c, large wall mirror, strip shaver socket, extractor and electric heater.\n\nBalcony: - \nEnjoying a glorious sunny orientation with views towards the Dublin Mountains.\n\nParking: - \nSecure designated underground parking space.\n\nService Charge: - \n2,917 plus a levy of 1,200 (current financial year 01/2026 12/2026)\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Exceptionally bright and spacious two-bedroom top-floor apartment</li><li> Very well-presented throughout with a warm, inviting feel</li><li> Glorious south-east facing orientation with excellent natural light</li><li> Secure designated underground parking space</li><li> Balcony access from both the living room and Bedroom 2</li><li> Generous living room with timber fireplace and inset electric fire</li><li> Well-fitted kitchen with Beko oven, ceramic hob, extractor hood and integrated dishwasher</li><li> Useful utility/storage closet plumbed for washing machine</li><li> Two spacious double bedrooms, both with built-in wardrobes</li><li> Master bedroom with en-suite shower room</li><li> Main bathroom with bath and shower attachment</li><li> Electric heating</li><li> Fibre broadband available</li><li> Telephone intercom and large hot press</li><li> Mature, well-maintained development in a highly convenient South Dublin location</ul>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
